igher inventories of certain new products to meet expected demands and we have import items which were purchased at higher levels to protect against potential tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/31/universal-forest-products-inc-ufpi-q2-2019-earning.aspx"},{"c":"UFPI 2019 Q2","e":"ufpi","d":"2019-07-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Matthew Missad","x":"We are making changes to our systems to better capture discretionary SG&A costs and looking at several ways to streamline operations which would reduce the rate of growth of operational SG&A expenses.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/31/universal-forest-products-inc-ufpi-q2-2019-earning.aspx"},{"c":"UFPI 2019 Q4","e":"ufpi","d":"2020-02-20","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Matthew J. Missad","x":"One is the -- I don't know how much is attributable to coronavirus to be honest, but in terms of different duties and tariffs, we are seeing a lot more interest in buying domestic product, which may have been stuff [Phonetic] purchased overseas before.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/20/universal-forest-products-inc-ufpi-q4-2019-earning.aspx"},{"c":"UFPI 2019 Q4","e":"ufpi","d":"2020-02-20","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Matthew J. Missad","x":"We look at that more as a pass-through type item.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/20/universal-forest-products-inc-ufpi-q4-2019-earning.aspx"},{"c":"UFPI 2019 Q4","e":"ufpi","d":"2020-02-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Matthew J. Missad","x":"I think for at least this year and probably part of next year, I don't expect that to be reduced a lot as a result of our restructuring process.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/20/universal-forest-products-inc-ufpi-q4-2019-earning.aspx"},{"c":"UFPI 2020 Q1","e":"ufpi","d":"2020-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Michael R. Cole","x":"We believe 50 basis points of the increase is due to the pass-through impact of lower lumber prices.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/07/universal-forest-products-inc-ufpi-q1-2020-earning.aspx"},{"c":"UFPI 2020 Q1","e":"ufpi","d":"2020-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Matthew J. Missad","x":"Our labor force has declined 10% with a combination of temporary labor, temporary layoffs, and some permanent layoffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/07/universal-forest-products-inc-ufpi-q1-2020-earning.aspx"},{"c":"UFPI 2020 Q1","e":"ufpi","d":"2020-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Matthew J. Missad","x":"We hope to be able to bring back all of our employees who are on temporary layoffs, assuming they're willing to come back.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/07/universal-forest-products-inc-ufpi-q1-2020-earning.aspx"},{"c":"UFPI 2020 Q3","e":"ufpi","d":"2020-10-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mike Cole","x":"I mentioned earlier what the price increase was in retail and that's predominantly the ProWood pressure-treated.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/22/universal-forest-products-inc-ufpi-q3-2020-earning/"},{"c":"UFPI 2020 Q4","e":"ufpi","d":"2021-02-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Julio Romero","x":"Okay, I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/ufp-industries-inc-ufpi-q4-2020-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"UFPI 2020 Q4","e":"ufpi","d":"2021-02-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Matthew J. Missad","x":"We have created a new path forward which include streamlining our operations team, exiting unprofitable product lines, consolidating facilities and sizing staffing levels based on actual, not anticipated sales volumes.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/ufp-industries-inc-ufpi-q4-2020-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"UFPI 2020 Q4","e":"ufpi","d":"2021-02-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Matthew J. Missad","x":"We have added more resources to our internal M&A team to help each business unit identify and negotiate acquisition opportunities, as well as streamlining the closing and post closing transitions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/ufp-industries-inc-ufpi-q4-2020-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"UFPI 2021 Q1","e":"ufpi","d":"2021-04-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Matthew J. Missad","x":"Margins have been impacted somewhat due to the resin price increases in Q1, but those costs are being passed along in Q2.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/21/ufp-industries-inc-ufpi-q1-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"UFPI 2021 Q1","e":"ufpi","d":"2021-04-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Matthew J. Missad","x":"I also think, there is some benefit from the tailwind of higher lumber prices, but as we said, we think, long-term, our strategy is to have those be more of a pass-through cost and try to get more efficient.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/21/ufp-industries-inc-ufpi-q1-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"UFPI 2021 Q1","e":"ufpi","d":"2021-04-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Matthew J. Missad","x":"Our rightsizing of the commercial construction business unit continues as planned and we have reached agreement in principle to sell one of our facilities and consolidate this business into our remaining locations.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/21/ufp-industries-inc-ufpi-q1-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"UFPI 2021 Q3","e":"ufpi","d":"2021-10-20","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Julio Romero","x":"And then last one for me and I'll pass it on is -- just given the current lumber environment, how conducive do you think that is to your inventory restock for '22?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/20/ufp-industries-inc-ufpi-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"UFPI 2025 Q2","e":"ufpi","d":"2025-07-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Will Schwartz","x":"News around duties on Canadian lumber and other tariffs has only created additional headwinds.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/ufp-industries-ufpi-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2025 Q2","e":"ufpi","d":"2025-07-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Will Schwartz","x":"Regardless of the outcome, we remain confident in our ability to navigate any potential tariff impacts.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/ufp-industries-ufpi-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2025 Q2","e":"ufpi","d":"2025-07-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Will Schwartz","x":"Operationally, we remain focused on maximizing capacity within our existing footprint and streamlining our cost structure.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/ufp-industries-ufpi-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2025 Q2","e":"ufpi","d":"2025-07-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Will Schwartz","x":"We have made great progress on our $60 million cost-out program and are on track to realize the full savings exiting 2026.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/07/ufp-industries-ufpi-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2026 Q1","e":"ufpi","d":"2026-04-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Michael Cole","x":"But the good news is that in April, as Will had indicated, that's when we started taking actions with our customers and now through freight surcharges and price increases on the products, depending on which approach the customers prefer, we're now beginning to pass that through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/30/ufp-ufpi-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2026 Q1","e":"ufpi","d":"2026-04-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"W. Andrew Carter","x":"What I wanted to ask is on the kind of inflation, the energy pass-through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/30/ufp-ufpi-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2026 Q1","e":"ufpi","d":"2026-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"William Schwartz","x":"On the cost side, we are actively mitigating higher costs and remain on track to deliver the remaining $25 million of our $60 million cost-out program by year-end with the potential to capture incremental savings beyond our initial targets.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/30/ufp-ufpi-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2026 Q1","e":"ufpi","d":"2026-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"William Schwartz","x":"Finally, our Commercial business continues to build on new products, new customer relationships and the benefits from prior restructuring actions to deliver improved results.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/30/ufp-ufpi-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2026 Q3","e":"ufpi","d":"2026-10-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mike Cole","x":"Pricing added 5%, reflecting higher lumber prices passed through to customers and programs in place to offset other inflationary pressures.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/ufp-industries-ufpi-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2026 Q3","e":"ufpi","d":"2026-10-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Andrew Carter","x":"I will pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/ufp-industries-ufpi-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2026 Q3","e":"ufpi","d":"2026-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mike Cole","x":"In retail, our financial priorities are clear: improve ProWood profitability by expanding its distribution of Deckorators products, achieve throughput and cost out targets primarily in composite decking, and keep growing sales of new value-added products like Arris trim and TrueFrame joists.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/ufp-industries-ufpi-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"UFPI 2026 Q3","e":"ufpi","d":"2026-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mike Cole","x":"We remain on track to meet or exceed our $60 million cost-out target, supported by capacity consolidations we completed last year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/ufp-industries-ufpi-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[35,1,6121,0,0,0,4205,1355],[36,1,4003,0,0,0,2990,700],[37,1,5630,0,0,0,4300,1011],[38,1,5204,0,0,0,3867,1102],[39,1,4950,0,0,0,3775,871],[40,1,6950,0,0,0,5241,1267],[41,1,6677,0,0,0,5199,1011],[43,1,6694,0,0,0,5004,1326],[44,1,8197,0,0,0,6440,1343],[45,1,7258,0,0,0,5292,1545],[46,1,6689,0,0,0,5296,1099],[47,1,6303,0,0,0,4783,1161],[62,1,6405,0,0,0,5060,1063],[65,1,6347,0,0,0,4998,1125],[67,1,8117,0,0,0,3613,3840]],"cinema":[[35,1,6121,0,0,0,4205,1355],[36,1,4003,0,0,0,2990,700],[37,1,5630,0,0,0,4300,1011],[38,1,5204,0,0,0,3867,1102],[39,1,4950,0,0,0,3775,871],[40,1,6950,0,0,0,5241,1267],[41,1,6677,0,0,0,5199,1011],[43,1,6694,0,0,0,5004,1326],[44,1,8197,0,0,0,6440,1343],[45,1,7258,0,0,0,5292,1545],[46,1,6689,0,0,0,5296,1099],[47,1,6303,0,0,0,4783,1161],[62,1,6405,0,0,0,5060,1063],[65,1,6347,0,0,0,4998,1125],[67,1,8117,0,0,0,3613,3840]],"imax":[[35,1,6121,0,0,0,4205,1355],[36,1,4003,0,0,0,2990,700],[37,1,5630,0,0,0,4300,1011],[38,1,5204,0,0,0,3867,1102],[39,1,4950,0,0,0,3775,871],[40,1,6950,0,0,0,5241,1267],[41,1,6677,0,0,0,5199,1011],[43,1,6694,0,0,0,5004,1326],[44,1,8197,0,0,0,6440,1343],[45,1,7258,0,0,0,5292,1545],[46,1,6689,0,0,0,5296,1099],[47,1,6303,0,0,0,4783,1161],[62,1,6405,0,0,0,5060,1063],[65,1,6347,0,0,0,4998,1125],[67,1,8117,0,0,0,3613,3840]],"streaming":[[35,1,6121,0,0,0,4205,1355],[36,1,4003,0,0,0,2990,700],[37,1,5630,0,0,0,4300,1011],[38,1,5204,0,0,0,3867,1102],[39,1,4950,0,0,0,3775,871],[40,1,6950,0,0,0,5241,1267],[41,1,66